WEBVTT

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.160
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.450
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.940
Polar 
 Bear's 
  Café

00:01:31.430 --> 00:01:34.430
Polar Bear Goes to the Zoo.

00:01:36.230 --> 00:01:37.400
Hey, Polar Bear.

00:01:38.690 --> 00:01:41.690
I'm a little bored, 
so give me a problem to solve.

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:42.870
Sure.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.580
Question 1:

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:48.820
"The T-intersection."

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:51.590
The legal name for this 
kind of intersection

00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:52.840
is not actually "T-intersection."

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:55.790
What is the proper name?

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:59.800
I'd prefer something a 
little less complicated.

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:05.270
There are many ways of 
manufacturing pre-washed rice.

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:05.270
Uncooked
rice

00:02:05.890 --> 00:02:09.050
But when using the NTWP 
manufacturing method,

00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:09.860
it's common—

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:12.090
Actually, never mind.

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:16.610
Oh, hey, Panda.

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:17.690
Welcome.

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:22.270
Would you like your usual, Panda?

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:30.470
What's wrong?

00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:31.900
Want a trivia question?

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:33.040
Instead of a trivia question,

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:38.370
why don't you come visit 
me at the zoo, Polar Bear?

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.430
What's this, all of a sudden?

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:45.320
I always come to visit you at work.

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:46.730
It's not fair.

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:49.360
But you're coming to the café as a customer.

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:53.090
I'm really popular with people, you know?

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:55.260
He's not listening.

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:58.300
Come visit me at the zoo at least once.

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:01.990
You'll be surprised at how popular I am.

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:04.950
You'll be surprised at how popular I am.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.350
Why'd you have to say it twice?

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:12.880
PANDA

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:12.880
Hello, Polar Bear?

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:16.420
I'm calling to remind you

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:18.150
to come to the zoo tomorrow.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:22.220
Please tell Mr. Penguin, too.

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:22.590
PANDA

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:25.930
Individual  Group

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:27.700
Panda

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:30.950
Good morning!

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:32.600
Good morning, Panda.

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:35.230
You're in good spirits today.

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:38.760
My friends are coming to see me today.

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:39.940
I see...

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:42.210
Oh, that's right!

00:03:42.210 --> 00:03:44.170
Full-time Panda has the day off today

00:03:44.170 --> 00:03:46.780
because he's visiting 
his daughter's class.

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:48.790
Oh, really?

00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:53.530
Wait, that means...

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:58.270
I'll be the only panda.

00:03:58.850 --> 00:04:00.990
<i>You're so cute, Mr. Panda!</i>

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:10.270
<i>Mr. Panda!</i>

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:14.600
<i>You're so cute, Panda!</i>

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:18.690
All right! I'll do my best!

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:28.780
How many?

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:31.730
Two...

00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:33.250
Animals, please.

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:37.170
So, this is the zoo.

00:04:37.820 --> 00:04:39.860
It's a lot bigger than I thought.

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:42.550
Let's go see Panda first.

00:04:45.170 --> 00:04:48.760
We will now start the 
polar bear feeding time.

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:52.270
Please enjoy watching the polar bear

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:54.020
dive into the water!

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:56.850
I want to go see! That sounds amazing!

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:59.250
What? You want to see that?

00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:02.760
You're a polar bear, right, Polar Bear?

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:07.490
You want to see a 
polar bear diving, Polar Bear?

00:05:08.090 --> 00:05:09.470
Let's go, let's go!

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:16.170
Panda!

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:19.900
Are you doing okay, working that hard?

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:21.510
Mr. Handa,

00:05:21.510 --> 00:05:25.020
when my friends come, 
please take our picture.

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:29.180
But it's strange,

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:32.620
They said they'd 
be here around 1pm,

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:34.280
but I don't see them anywhere.

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:40.130
Polar Bear Hall

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:40.130
Welcome to the 
Polar Bear Hall.

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:39.430
We can't go in here, Polar Bear.

00:05:39.430 --> 00:05:40.150
Look.

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:41.500
What?

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:43.980
It says you can't enter.

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:48.950
We apologize for the inconvenience, 
but polar bears are not allowed 
in the Polar Bear Hall.

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:46.880
"We apologize for the 
inconvenience, but polar bears

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:48.870
are not allowed in the 
Polar Bear Hall.

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:51.450
It confuses them!

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:51.450
It confuses them!"

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:56.770
If we sneak in quietly, 
they'll never even notice.

00:05:57.420 --> 00:05:59.750
No... I think we're pretty obvious.

00:06:06.390 --> 00:06:08.220
Wow! That's incredible!

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:09.300
A polar bear!

00:06:09.530 --> 00:06:11.510
Hey, hey!

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:14.470
The sign clearly says 
no polar bears allowed!

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:15.840
It's really troublesome.

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:19.940
Um... This is actually a stuffed animal.

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:23.400
It was just moving!

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:25.290
There's no way it's stuffed!

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:30.570
Why aren't they here yet?

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:32.830
Um, I'm going to go now.

00:06:33.340 --> 00:06:34.870
Call me when they get here.

00:06:34.890 --> 00:06:37.310
Polar Bear Hall

00:06:34.890 --> 00:06:37.310
Welcome to the 
Polar Bear Hall.

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:37.330
See? We got in trouble.

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:40.490
I said we'd get in trouble.

00:06:40.490 --> 00:06:43.350
Then let's go see Panda.

00:06:43.350 --> 00:06:44.460
Okay.

00:06:48.820 --> 00:06:50.950
You're so cute, Panda!

00:06:52.410 --> 00:06:53.840
You're so cute!

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:56.280
Panda!

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:00.770
Sorry we're late, Panda!

00:07:04.180 --> 00:07:05.200
Huh?

00:07:05.640 --> 00:07:08.320
Hey, Panda!

00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:15.330
He's asleep.

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:17.510
Panda!

00:07:17.510 --> 00:07:18.870
Wake up!

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:27.670
He's laughing...

00:07:28.470 --> 00:07:29.970
Panda!

00:07:30.270 --> 00:07:31.230
Hey!

00:07:31.230 --> 00:07:33.560
Panda!

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:38.390
It's no use.

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:41.350
Let's go somewhere else.

00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:45.940
I envy the fact that he's 
allowed to sleep at work.

00:07:48.430 --> 00:07:52.110
Hey, I think I just heard Mr. Penguin!

00:07:53.310 --> 00:07:55.400
Aw, he's not here.

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:00.750
Oh, Mr. Handa.

00:08:01.130 --> 00:08:02.410
Yes?

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:04.310
Did my friends happen to stop by?

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:07.210
I didn't see them.

00:08:07.690 --> 00:08:10.040
Make sure you take our picture, 'kay?

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:12.170
Sure, sure...

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:17.370
Welcome to the Seal Hall.

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:15.440
Hey, the Seal Hall!

00:08:15.920 --> 00:08:17.390
Let's go!

00:08:17.410 --> 00:08:21.810
We apologize for the inconvenience, 
but polar bears are not allowed 
in the Seal Hall

00:08:18.550 --> 00:08:21.720
"Polar bears are not allowed...

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:25.250
It scares the seals!

00:08:22.690 --> 00:08:25.270
It scares the seals!"

00:08:26.490 --> 00:08:27.880
There ya go.

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:32.600
No one will even notice.

00:08:33.140 --> 00:08:34.990
No, we're pretty obvious.

00:08:36.420 --> 00:08:38.180
Don't worry, I won't eat you.

00:08:38.180 --> 00:08:39.700
A polar bear!

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:43.620
Even though I know I won't eat one,

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:47.270
I still get a little 
excited when I see one.

00:08:48.190 --> 00:08:53.030
Let's leave before your 
natural instincts take over.

00:08:53.030 --> 00:08:54.490
Hey, hey!

00:08:55.540 --> 00:08:58.720
The sign clearly said 
no polar bears allowed!

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:01.930
Oh, this is just a rug.

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:05.830
See? Look!

00:09:05.830 --> 00:09:08.330
It's so fluffy!

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:11.320
Wow.

00:09:11.660 --> 00:09:13.740
We can't seem to pull one 
over on them.

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:14.830
Jeez.

00:09:15.460 --> 00:09:18.370
Panda might actually be awake now.

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:23.930
Hey, Panda!

00:09:27.350 --> 00:09:29.110
He's laughing again.

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:32.730
It's amazing that he can 
sleep in that position.

00:09:32.730 --> 00:09:35.130
I actually admire him for that.

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:37.590
Excuse me,

00:09:38.080 --> 00:09:41.590
are you Panda's friends?

00:09:41.590 --> 00:09:42.680
Yes, we are.

00:09:43.240 --> 00:09:45.220
Could I take a picture?

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:47.720
He asked me to take one.

00:09:57.550 --> 00:10:01.780
I wonder if Mr. Giraffe 
will come to my café.

00:10:02.300 --> 00:10:05.260
No, I don't think he can get in.

00:10:07.610 --> 00:10:10.340
Let's look around the other places, too.

00:10:10.340 --> 00:10:11.680
Okay.

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:16.010
So, where did you want to go?

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:20.720
Oh, how about the Penguin Corner?

00:10:22.380 --> 00:10:26.520
You should join in their 
acrobatics act, Mr. Penguin.

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:29.510
I'm terrible with exercise.

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:31.730
Hey, there.

00:10:33.300 --> 00:10:35.010
Oh, hello, Mr. Llama.

00:10:35.490 --> 00:10:37.490
What brings you here today?

00:10:37.950 --> 00:10:42.430
We came to see Panda, but he's asleep.

00:10:42.430 --> 00:10:44.200
He's awake sometimes.

00:10:44.630 --> 00:10:45.660
Oh, okay.

00:10:46.690 --> 00:10:49.590
Panda should be awake by now.

00:10:49.590 --> 00:10:50.670
Let's go look.

00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:57.760
He's asleep, again.

00:10:58.340 --> 00:11:01.140
And he looks even more shameless.

00:11:01.610 --> 00:11:06.470
I wonder what exactly 
Panda wanted us to see.

00:11:06.470 --> 00:11:09.980
That panda's so boring. 
All he does is sleep.

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:11.290
Yeah, let's go!

00:11:16.010 --> 00:11:18.190
"Popular," huh?

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:24.270
Hey, he's laughing again.

00:11:26.300 --> 00:11:28.590
I was waiting the whole day.

00:11:28.590 --> 00:11:30.820
Why didn't you come?

00:11:30.820 --> 00:11:33.150
Actually, we came by quite a few times.

00:11:33.150 --> 00:11:34.340
Really?

00:11:34.340 --> 00:11:35.670
We were there!

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:37.790
Right, Mr. Llama?

00:11:37.790 --> 00:11:39.880
We met at the zoo today, right?

00:11:40.380 --> 00:11:41.720
We did.

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:44.720
See? We did go.

00:11:45.940 --> 00:11:49.080
Why didn't you come see me?

00:11:49.080 --> 00:11:51.270
I just said we did!

00:11:51.970 --> 00:11:54.980
You spent that much time 
watching Mr. Llama?

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:58.110
I'm trying to tell you, 
we went to see you, too!

00:11:59.500 --> 00:12:03.460
I wonder why we didn't 
see each other, then.

00:12:03.460 --> 00:12:06.680
It's because you were 
asleep the whole time.

00:12:08.110 --> 00:12:09.840
You should have woken me up.

00:12:09.840 --> 00:12:11.470
You didn't wake up!

00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:18.500
And Mr. Handa even said 
he would take pictures...

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:20.840
He did.

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:26.050
Wow, you really did come!

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:28.990
That's what I've been saying.

00:12:32.440 --> 00:12:36.610
I'm so cute even when I'm sleeping.

00:12:37.590 --> 00:12:39.430
Hey, hey.

00:12:39.430 --> 00:12:41.910
Which sleeping face do you like best?

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:45.560
Could I get another, Polar Bear?

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:52.960
Polar 
 Bear's 
  Café

00:12:49.470 --> 00:12:51.940
Panda's Problems.

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:55.150
Miss Sasako,

00:12:55.150 --> 00:12:57.840
how do you feel about men
who like meat and potato stew?

00:12:59.570 --> 00:13:01.670
I'd rather not answer 
right now, if that's okay.

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:03.530
That's fine.

00:13:05.170 --> 00:13:07.200
That was standoffish.

00:13:08.590 --> 00:13:14.560
You know, I still can't figure 
out this "act naturally" thing.

00:13:15.150 --> 00:13:17.020
<i>Just act naturally.</i>

00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:21.450
No matter how much I think about it, 
I can't find the answer.

00:13:22.560 --> 00:13:26.530
What does it mean to act naturally, 
Mr. Full-time Panda?

00:13:34.340 --> 00:13:35.710
He's asleep!

00:13:38.230 --> 00:13:39.710
Hey, Mr. Handa,

00:13:39.710 --> 00:13:42.250
what does it mean to "act naturally"?

00:13:43.600 --> 00:13:47.680
You said it yourself, "just act naturally."

00:13:48.550 --> 00:13:52.140
I think the act of acting 
naturally is "acting natural."

00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:55.330
Could you give me an example?

00:13:58.770 --> 00:14:00.520
Something like this.

00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:04.750
That's not cute.

00:14:12.560 --> 00:14:15.720
What does it mean to "act naturally"?

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:18.080
Something like this?

00:14:19.180 --> 00:14:22.540
I don't know if that's acting 
natural or not, but it is cute.

00:14:23.600 --> 00:14:24.880
How about this?

00:14:25.810 --> 00:14:26.840
It's cute.

00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:29.180
And this?

00:14:30.290 --> 00:14:32.640
We get it. You're cute.

00:14:33.690 --> 00:14:35.940
I know.

00:14:35.940 --> 00:14:38.550
I keep getting called cute,

00:14:38.550 --> 00:14:41.260
but I still don't know what to do.

00:14:41.260 --> 00:14:42.610
How nice.

00:14:42.610 --> 00:14:45.150
I wish someone would call me cute.

00:14:45.990 --> 00:14:48.970
All I'm doing is lounging around.

00:14:48.970 --> 00:14:51.990
You always look like you're 
having fun. I'm jealous.

00:14:52.980 --> 00:14:54.420
Mr. Otter?

00:14:54.420 --> 00:14:57.700
You know I break shellfish 
on my tummy, right?

00:14:57.700 --> 00:14:59.810
It's harder than it looks.

00:14:59.810 --> 00:15:01.500
It hurts my tummy.

00:15:06.860 --> 00:15:09.340
I'm banging a rock on 
my tummy, Miss Sasako.

00:15:09.730 --> 00:15:10.730
I'm sorry?

00:15:10.730 --> 00:15:13.930
You should try banging 
a rock on your tummy.

00:15:22.250 --> 00:15:23.840
It would hurt, right?

00:15:23.840 --> 00:15:25.460
Yes...

00:15:25.460 --> 00:15:27.650
Then you shouldn't try 
breaking it on your tummy.

00:15:28.060 --> 00:15:30.610
But the audience loves seeing that.

00:15:31.690 --> 00:15:34.330
Why don't you give up that act?

00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:36.370
It's not really an act.

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:37.790
It's more of a trait.

00:15:38.270 --> 00:15:41.000
I think it's fine since it's cute.

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:45.230
It's cute, but my tummy's had enough.

00:15:45.230 --> 00:15:49.130
Since we're on the topic 
of cute, I'm cute, too.

00:15:49.560 --> 00:15:50.840
Mr. Koala?

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:56.830
I'm cutely eating eucalyptus, 
but I'm at my limit.

00:15:56.830 --> 00:15:58.060
I'm sick of it.

00:16:03.210 --> 00:16:07.190
I eat about one kilogram 
of that stuff a day.

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:09.920
You'd get teary-eyed, too, 
if you had to do it.

00:16:09.920 --> 00:16:11.740
I know! I totally get you!

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:14.000
You, too, Anteater?

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:15.820
I don't like the name Anteater!

00:16:19.140 --> 00:16:22.240
I don't want to eat 
 only ants all the time!

00:16:22.240 --> 00:16:23.040
I'm sick of them!

00:16:23.510 --> 00:16:24.760
Do you know how it feels

00:16:24.760 --> 00:16:26.820
to have to eat ants all 
the time, Miss Sasako?!

00:16:26.820 --> 00:16:28.000
I'm sorry?!

00:16:29.180 --> 00:16:30.710
I can't say that I do.

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:33.290
Well, you are an anteater...

00:16:33.290 --> 00:16:34.840
You don't have much of a choice.

00:16:34.840 --> 00:16:39.200
I know, but I want to 
eat other things, too!

00:16:39.200 --> 00:16:40.430
Other things?

00:16:40.820 --> 00:16:42.410
Like what?

00:16:42.410 --> 00:16:44.520
You know, like ramen!

00:16:50.420 --> 00:16:53.510
But I don't think you 
can eat chashu pork.

00:16:53.510 --> 00:16:56.310
You don't have to be concerned 
with the little things.

00:16:56.310 --> 00:16:59.110
At least people look at you.

00:17:00.860 --> 00:17:02.180
Mr. Llama?

00:17:02.180 --> 00:17:05.810
Everyone pretty much
 passes right by me.

00:17:05.810 --> 00:17:07.960
Did you even know I was there?

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:10.460
Come to think of it...

00:17:11.590 --> 00:17:13.980
When we went to the zoo...

00:17:13.980 --> 00:17:16.220
We did pretty much pass right by.

00:17:16.220 --> 00:17:19.490
See? That's how it is, being a llama.

00:17:20.750 --> 00:17:23.370
I wish people would look longer,

00:17:23.370 --> 00:17:26.600
and form huge lines
 to tell me what they think of me.

00:17:26.750 --> 00:17:28.650
End of line

00:17:28.790 --> 00:17:30.980
<i>Wow, it's a llama!</i>

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:32.440
<i>Look, it's eating grass!</i>

00:17:32.440 --> 00:17:34.150
<i>Hurry! Take a picture!</i>

00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:36.360
You just eat grass?

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:38.120
That's a little boring.

00:17:38.120 --> 00:17:40.410
Are you a donkey, Mr. Llama?

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:42.450
As I said, I'm a llama.

00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:44.950
If you had to compare, 
I'm closer to a camel.

00:17:44.950 --> 00:17:46.090
Do you have a hump?

00:17:46.090 --> 00:17:47.290
I do not.

00:17:47.290 --> 00:17:48.470
Um...

00:17:48.470 --> 00:17:52.050
Can you do any tricks or anything?

00:17:52.050 --> 00:17:54.090
Just eating grass.

00:17:54.090 --> 00:17:57.800
Other than that, 
my eyelashes are very long.

00:18:01.380 --> 00:18:04.330
I hope you get that huge line of yours.

00:18:05.090 --> 00:18:07.880
Being looked at isn't all that great.

00:18:07.880 --> 00:18:08.980
Mr. Tapir.

00:18:09.330 --> 00:18:14.030
I'm rumored to be an animal 
that eats dreams,

00:18:14.030 --> 00:18:17.350
but everyone who sees me is unimpressed.

00:18:17.350 --> 00:18:19.930
What kind of animal 
eats dreams, anyway?

00:18:19.930 --> 00:18:22.230
They're setting the bar much too high.

00:18:22.230 --> 00:18:25.960
Now, now. You're better 
off than the sea cow.

00:18:25.960 --> 00:18:28.540
They get compared to mermaids.

00:18:30.720 --> 00:18:34.030
<i>Mommy, where's the mermaid?</i>

00:18:36.130 --> 00:18:38.620
Everyone who sees it 
doesn't know what to say.

00:18:38.620 --> 00:18:39.900
Right?

00:18:39.900 --> 00:18:42.050
Please don't ask me.

00:18:43.870 --> 00:18:45.330
You have a point.

00:18:45.800 --> 00:18:49.760
If you compare me to Ms. Sea Cow, 
I'm probably better off.

00:18:49.760 --> 00:18:51.060
Me, too...

00:18:51.850 --> 00:18:53.600
Sloth.

00:18:53.600 --> 00:18:57.240
I'm not associated with the zoo, but...

00:18:57.790 --> 00:19:04.360
People think I just hang 
from a tree all day.

00:19:05.490 --> 00:19:06.830
And in reality?

00:19:07.800 --> 00:19:10.120
I do in reality...

00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:13.750
But it's hard. 
My arms tingle.

00:19:14.770 --> 00:19:19.340
Have you ever hung from a 
tree all day, Miss Sasako?

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:22.340
I can't say that I have.

00:19:22.670 --> 00:19:26.170
I guess Sloth isn't really a sloth.

00:19:26.170 --> 00:19:27.560
He's a really hard worker.

00:19:28.940 --> 00:19:31.020
Tell me more.

00:19:31.510 --> 00:19:34.380
Apparently everyone has problems.

00:19:34.380 --> 00:19:36.110
I have a problem too.

00:19:36.410 --> 00:19:39.570
You see, I have this penguin that I like.

00:19:40.070 --> 00:19:42.870
Don't tell anyone though, okay?

00:19:44.100 --> 00:19:48.690
It seems that there isn't an 
end to everyone's problems.

00:19:48.690 --> 00:19:50.270
You're right.

00:19:50.270 --> 00:19:51.580
No kidding.

00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:53.560
Hey, listen to me.

00:19:53.560 --> 00:19:55.880
Don't you have any 
problems, Mr. Polar Bear?

00:19:56.650 --> 00:19:57.800
I do.

00:19:58.010 --> 00:20:01.370
Really? You do? That's unexpected.

00:20:01.370 --> 00:20:05.400
I've been asked if I 
wanted to become an idol,

00:20:05.400 --> 00:20:08.080
but fitting that in
with my studies would be hard.

00:20:08.790 --> 00:20:10.630
There you go, lying again.

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:12.990
How about you, Miss Sasako?

00:20:14.180 --> 00:20:15.370
I don't have any.

00:20:15.370 --> 00:20:16.320
Not even one?

00:20:16.320 --> 00:20:16.980
Indeed.

00:20:19.890 --> 00:20:20.570
What is it?

00:20:21.120 --> 00:20:23.780
I was wondering if Hina dolls should

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:26.990
go with the burnable or 
non-burnable garbage.

00:20:27.540 --> 00:20:30.040
How about we discuss that later?

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:35.630
Every time I go to the bakery, 
I think about it.

00:20:37.410 --> 00:20:40.420
Listen, don't tell anyone, okay?

00:20:40.420 --> 00:20:44.310
I keep trying to figure 
out how to ask her out.

00:20:44.980 --> 00:20:46.850
What do you think, Panda?

00:20:49.270 --> 00:20:51.850
Hey, this is no laughing matter.

00:20:54.390 --> 00:20:55.810
He's asleep!

00:20:58.240 --> 00:20:59.530
Hm...

00:21:00.310 --> 00:21:02.190
I wonder how long he's been asleep.

00:21:02.770 --> 00:21:05.950
Probably somewhere right after 
the talk of chashu pork.

00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:08.870
So somewhere at the beginning 
of the conversation.

00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:14.840
Oh, Mr. Polar Bear.

00:21:14.840 --> 00:21:16.970
Could I get seconds, please?

00:21:16.970 --> 00:21:17.670
Sure.

00:21:21.240 --> 00:21:23.380
"Acting naturally," huh?

00:21:24.110 --> 00:21:26.410
I wonder what I should do?

00:21:27.980 --> 00:21:31.360
Panda is totally acting 
naturally right now.

00:21:31.360 --> 00:21:32.470
Indeed he is.

00:21:38.730 --> 00:21:40.000
Welcome.

00:21:44.020 --> 00:21:46.270
I'm so tired today.

00:21:46.910 --> 00:21:48.160
Hey, Panda.

00:21:48.930 --> 00:21:49.660
What?

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:54.000
I've been thinking since then...

00:21:54.570 --> 00:21:58.670
"Acting naturally" for you is

00:21:58.670 --> 00:22:01.850
being in the place 
you can relax the most.

00:22:03.540 --> 00:22:04.670
Oh!

00:22:05.150 --> 00:22:05.990
Meaning―

00:22:05.990 --> 00:22:08.340
Never mind that, Mr. Penguin.

00:22:09.430 --> 00:22:13.350
I bought new panda merchandise.

00:22:13.350 --> 00:22:15.430
What do you think I should put in here?

00:22:20.370 --> 00:22:22.150
How about a meat bun?

00:23:54.970 --> 00:24:24.500
Next Time

00:23:57.540 --> 00:23:59.590
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin!

00:23:59.590 --> 00:24:01.490
Is it true that Polar Bear's Café

00:24:01.490 --> 00:24:03.790
is being turned into a 
parking lot next week?

00:24:03.790 --> 00:24:05.790
I didn't hear a rumor like that.

00:24:05.790 --> 00:24:07.800
Are you sure you haven't 
had plastic surgery?

00:24:07.800 --> 00:24:09.000
I did not.

00:24:09.000 --> 00:24:11.600
I ask again, what makes you think I did?

00:24:11.600 --> 00:24:13.550
Polar Bear, could you finish it?

00:24:13.550 --> 00:24:14.730
Sure.

00:24:14.730 --> 00:24:16.430
Next time on Polar Bear's...

00:24:17.770 --> 00:24:19.100
Hm...

00:24:20.000 --> 00:24:24.500
Obsessed with Smart phones
Super Fun Driving Lesson

00:24:20.150 --> 00:24:22.040
It's "Café." Did you actually forget?

00:24:22.040 --> 00:24:23.290
Enjoy!
